rt":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"key":"kOJJEyRwpM"},{"type":"cite","url":"https://doi.org/10.21105/joss.01797","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mansour ","key":"NzdHpIpPWS"},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"et al.","key":"gfdjgKuPe8"}],"key":"uWXfbKn7Cy"},{"type":"text","value":" (2020)","key":"Z3NMlr3ZX1"}],"kind":"narrative","label":"Mansour_2020","identifier":"https://doi.org/10.21105/joss.01797","enumerator":"2","key":"n3k5EisE0A"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"key":"NyisGtk5eh"}],"key":"NcmwgGSD0K"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pip Install","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"OEgILhraMO"}],"identifier":"pip-install","label":"Pip Install","html_id":"pip-install","implicit":true,"key":"eJDz9EN7Ja"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"While Underworld2 is a Python API, it relies on a complex stack of C libraries to provide much of its core functionality. Statically typed languages such as C are generally orders of magnitude faster than dynamically typed languages (such as Python) and therefore are usually the best choice for numerically heavy routines. Indeed, most computational Python libraries (such as ","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"TP6FUYK20L"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"numpy","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"wkoMvtz42G"},{"type":"text","value":" and ","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"MAfIZUKA1B"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scipy","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"Hr9yBz33LE"},{"type":"text","value":" use Python for high level orchestration, but outsource all expensive computations to statically typed layers, and ","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"t8vTBy56Px"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"underworld","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"FkDU8O0Lkf"},{"type":"text","value":" is no different. While this design is critical to achieving high performance, it does come with the necessary complexity of generating  library binaries for each platform ","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"KuzsVdqZ0L"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"underworld","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"j9iBPCjxiF"},{"type":"text","value":" needs to run on. ABI compatible third party libraries (such as ","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"hRVJlScMYv"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"petsc","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"h4Q1EWPwEZ"},{"type":"text","value":") also need to be created if not available.","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"bwuSLZ6VDe"}],"key":"grjMtgwip9"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Underworld team’s solution to this problem is ","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"wrzTeyXVXw"},{"type":"link","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OS-level%5Fvirtualisation","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"container virtualisation,","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"EqywXsOClk"}],"urlSource":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OS-level%5Fvirtualisation","data":{"page":"OS-level%5Fvirtualisation","wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/","lang":"en"},"internal":false,"protocol":"wiki","key":"hR13ECfMfF"},{"type":"text","value":" and in particular ","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"d1f8VZc0tz"},{"type":"link","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Docker%5F%28software%29","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Docker","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"ESn6VON7Qp"}],"urlSource":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Docker%5F%28software%29","data":{"page":"Docker%5F%28software%29","wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/","lang":"en"},"internal":false,"protocol":"wiki","key":"ppuD7U1hn7"},{"type":"text","value":". Containers allow us to generate an image containing the entire runtime stack required to run ","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"R1wGoXRBtS"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"underworld","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"daHwbVOKd4"},{"type":"text","value":", along with all other peripheral tools our users usually wish to run (such as ","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"NJdR8sGu22"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Jupyter","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"PSO3p24FIE"},{"type":"text","value":"). Containers also provide portability, with the single image being able to be utilised on any platform where a Linux kernel can be made available (which includes OS X and Windows).  Indeed there are many other advantages to using containers, such as reproducibility, the ability to switch versions trivially, and even HPC amenability is becoming realistic via tools such as ","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"FW5f8xBPy7"},{"type":"link","url":"https://github.com/NERSC/shifter","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shifter","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"gKRh9rElTf"}],"urlSource":"https://github.com/NERSC/shifter","error":true,"key":"wmmVUfaKtK"},{"type":"text","value":" and ","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"wul8Ybehaf"},{"type":"link","url":"https://singularity.lbl.gov/","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Singularity","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"q28FGaX0kr"}],"urlSource":"https://singularity.lbl.gov/","key":"u0pQrJNcha"},{"type":"text","value":" (with potential benefits over bare metal for Python in particular).","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"xxxdWAsERf"}],"key":"THNAxZ0zKI"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"However there are certainly shortcomings to container usage. Foremost, it presents a significant learning curve for new users, particularly those not familiar with virtualisation. While front-ends such as Kitematic go a long way to hide much of this difficulty, users will probably still require some understanding of the underlying paradigms for frictionless operation. Image size can also be of annoyance, with ","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"msUPXam9TG"},{"type":"link","url":"https://hub.docker.com/r/underworldcode/underworld2/tags","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"our complete images weighing in at almost 1GB,","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"C8Yskunpdg"}],"urlSource":"https://hub.docker.com/r/underworldcode/underworld2/tags","key":"AAim9ke3oU"},{"type":"text","value":" and over 2GB when uncompressed. Finally, running inside a virtualised environment isolates ","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"rCiuopVtFz"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"underworld","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"pTMt4XOtoz"},{"type":"text","value":" from the host and its software, such as locally installed Python modules and tools such as IDEs.","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"rVriwamzIK"}],"key":"Km8pjNkFB1"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"It is therefore also nice to have the option of a natively installed ","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"JZ8IZHUz3I"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"underworld","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"LLZYc7uq3w"},{"type":"text","value":" module. We have always provided minimal compilation instructions to allow users to generate local ","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"v1L1fSUR1f"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"underworld","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"nsKuliP0E3"},{"type":"text","value":" builds, but the expertise required to successfully compile ","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"pRT4rFs9Ei"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"underworld","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"XtODRRnHAm"},{"type":"text","value":" and its dependencies generally restricted this to power users. However in recent times the installation of third party libraries has become easier, and ","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"n8cZNbikl0"},{"type":"link","url":"https://github.